OL,3,GNEWSAScotland has right to decide
OL,4,Aconstitutional future, new Scottish
OL,5,ALabour leader says
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe new leader of Scottish Labour has
OL,8,Fbacked the country's right to decide
OL,9,Fits constitutional future.
OL,11,FMichael Marra supported that position
OL,12,Fin a non-binding vote at Holyrood,
OL,13,Fthough Labour remains opposed to
OL,14,Findependence and another referendum.
OL,16,FMarra told parliament there had
OL,17,F"always" been a route to a referendum -
OL,18,Fbut said the government had failed to
OL,19,Fbuild an "overwhelming" case for it.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
